## Workflow boundaries

- Keep the default subject open; `subject_policy.default_subjects` must remain empty.
- Protect the input subject, identity, and user constraints before applying layout or style.
- List only permitted visual changes in `style_projection.allowed_axes`.
- Places, people, objects, and stories come from the user input or an explicit selection; never hard-code them into the default prompt.
- For external projects, record only links and license information. Do not copy their skills, prompts, examples, or brand assets.

## Four ways to use it

1. Give this directory to an image-capable Agent together with your input and output goal.
2. Copy the constraints from `workflow.yaml`, replace the subject and aspect ratio, and keep the protection rules.
3. Give the workflow to an API-capable image Agent after configuring your own API key.
4. With a local model and ComfyUI, connect the workflow rules, reference manifest, and output size to separate nodes.

Confirm the rights to the input before generation. After generation, check that the subject was not replaced, no unrequested fixed object appeared, and the output matches the selected aspect ratio.
